# AWS Config custom policy rule (Guard runtime: guard-2.x.x)
# Description: Accounts tagged purpose=<tagValue> must be in the approved OU subtree.
# Deployed as: orggov-account-approved-parent-ou  (management account, us-east-1)
# Scope:       AWS::Organizations::Account   Trigger: configuration changes (periodic not supported)
#
# Accounts tagged purpose=<tagValue> must sit anywhere under the approved OU subtree.
# Parameter:   tagValue -> e.g. governed   (single value - console-safe)
#
# Notes (verified):
#  - Parameters are read with CONFIG_RULE_PARAMETERS.<key>; other names fail the whole rule
#    with InvalidPropertyReference.
#  - The tag KEY is literal (Guard 2.x has no dynamic key lookup); the VALUE is a parameter.
#  - Regex must be literal in Guard 2.x (cannot come from a parameter). Write "/" as \x2F;
#    "\/" is a parse error. The trailing \x2F prevents lookalike-ID matches.
#  - Field names are API casing (Paths, ParentIds) - NOT the camelCase shown in the console timeline.
#  - Untagged accounts SKIP -> NOT_APPLICABLE in Config.
#  - Approved subtree: o-exampleorgid / r-exmp / ou-exmp-approved and everything below it - EDIT per organization.
rule tagged_account_in_approved_ou when
    resourceType == "AWS::Organizations::Account"
    tags.purpose exists
    tags.purpose == CONFIG_RULE_PARAMETERS.tagValue {
    configuration.Paths[*] == /^o-exampleorgid\x2Fr-exmp\x2Fou-exmp-approved\x2F/
        <<Account carries the governed tag but is not under the approved OU subtree>>
}
